A||||3||Shiner||Aero Rocker Panel Removal and Installation||||5||
Z||000000||Shiner||09-12-2000||03:03 AM||||Working on the cars tommorow again.  I need to transplant an aero rocker from an '86 SE to an '87 GT.  Any suggestions or help?  I took a quick look, and it seems like at least ten rivets are holding the sucker on.  Somebody please help me out here, my Hayne's manual sucks, and I don't want to damage my rocker ;(||||reg||5
Z||000001||mrfiero||09-12-2000||04:09 AM||||I use an old T-10 or T-15 Torx screwdriver as a punch.....drive the center of the rivet through and then pry the rest of the rivet out or use a flat blade screwdriver as a chisel and pound it with a hammer from the side (breaks it in half).....either way works and you should have all of the rivets out in a matter of minutes.<P>Hopefully this isn't to vague.....good luck.<P><BR>  ||||reg||10
Z||000002||HugGRRRFiero||09-12-2000||08:15 AM||||  For the rivets along the top face I use a punch and hammer like mrfiero and punch the hardened pin out in the center.  You can chisel the head off, but I like to drill the head of the rivet off.  It creates a bit more of a mess with shavings, but if you drill carefully you won't damage the rocker.  For the plastic rivets along the bottom flange I just used an allen wrench with a handle to poke thru the hole and drive the pin out for those.  Hope this helps...<P>Brent||||reg||1
Z||000003||286SE'S||09-12-2000||01:15 PM||||Besides the one screw in each wheel well, there are also clips holding it to the effects sections on the front and rear fenders. One in front and three in the rear. Don't use a screwdriver to detach these, use a very thin tool like a narrow putty knife. A screwdriver will gouge up the soft plastic. <BR>I just pulled one off a car at the parts yard and not knowing what held it one, unhooked the fender effects from the top and looked down to see the clips. <BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
